WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.760
My best friend tried to kill me with her vehicle.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.860
I was on life support for three weeks.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:12.200
I'm still trying to understand why she did it.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.440
She ruined my life and she only got five years probation.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.880
[somber background music]

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.760
I took $100 from my dad's wallet.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.500
He found out and confronted me and my brother.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:47.120
I quickly put the money in my brother's drawer.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.900
My dad found it and kicked him out of the house.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.020
That was a year ago and we haven't heard much since.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.400
He won't answer my calls or texts.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:04.000
My friend committed suicide last year and I was the last person he tried calling.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:07.740
If I took the time and answered, he might still be here today.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:14.180
My little brother knocked his bowl of ramen while watching TV.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.360
My father blamed it on me, and after I tried explaining myself

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:20.680
he started slapping me until my glasses fell on the floor and broke.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.920
My mother and my brother did nothing.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.180
Later my mom said,

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:29.400
"If people ask how you broke your glasses, tell them it was because you fell on the ground."

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.140
Wow

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:35.680
I kept the fact that my dad was cheating on my mom with another woman.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.140
I should be a lot more mad at my dad.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.500
But for some reason,

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:44.300
I'm so guilt-ridden and angry at myself for hurting the most important person in my life.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:48.820
I feel like whatever I do, I can't make it up to my mom.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:54.020
It's a lot more difficult of a decision,

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.480
I think, than people may realize.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:02.160
Maybe she sees that, and they divorce, and it tears apart your whole family.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.700
Or maybe she doesn't believe it at all,

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:06.740
and then you just become

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:09.140
the, the bad guy

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:12.620
At first, I was not believed about

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:15.480
My father getting involved with a lady,

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.360
and speaking about it helped cause a lot of drama in my family.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:22.500
But you shouldn't feel,

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:24.680
Guilty

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:30.840
And you always have to remember that you can't blame yourself for things that other people are doing.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:36.560
I was outed as a lesbian by one of my closest friends to teachers at my Catholic school.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.660
I was kicked out of that school in the middle of my eighth-grade year.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:45.860
So, in college, I met this person.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:48.180
In secret they told me, that

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.900
they were discovering they were transgender.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.360
And they asked me not to tell anybody.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:54.660
And I broke that promise.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.880
Got an email from this person,

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:00.180
saying that I violated their trust, and that I

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:03.800
should never speak to them again.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.300
And I really regret,

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:09.120
sharing that information because it was not my information to tell.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:11.639
This person was being vulnerable with me and I violated their trust,

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:12.820
and I'm never gonna get that back.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.440
My mom passed away a few years ago

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:19.720
and every day it feels like my memories of her get blurrier.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:22.760
I feel guilty and mad at myself for forgetting her.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:32.700
My dad died from a stroke caused by complications from long-standing blood pressure problems.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.660
We were fighting a lot those days and were barely speaking when he passed.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:42.320
I fully believed that stress of our relationship is what caused the stroke and killed him.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:44.780
That's

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:47.080
really hard to go through.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.520
I don't think you should be blaming yourself.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:53.660
Honestly, time would heal most things.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:56.500
Journaling has helped.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:04:01.840
Talking to, if you have your mother figure in your life, just being able to

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.600
really get your thoughts out.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:07.080
So that you're not choked up with all that guilt inside.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.420
Just let it come out of you.

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:16.120
As a child, I was taking advantage of sexually by multiple men in my family.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:21.260
At age 15, when a school counselor heard about a specific uncle touching me,

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:23.800
she called the police and my mother.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.760
What hurt the most was when my mother was angry at me instead.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:31.600
I became disowned in my own home for years.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:36.680
It's especially hard, when

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:40.700
You don't want to talk about it, and you don't want anybody to find out

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:44.020
because you have no idea what's gonna happen.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:49.840
And then, you finally get the courage to say something, and it just ends up horrible.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:51.520
I'm sorry.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:52.980
I understand.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:57.060
And it does help to talk about it.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.660
Having people around you that support you,

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:01.840
and that you can trust is very important.

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.240
Even talking to someone about

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:06.980
things like a therapist, it helps.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.600
Even though it seems like it won't,

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:11.320
at some point it's going to get better.

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:17.520
I tried to kill myself the same night after me and my mother fought.

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:21.840
I went to my school to ask for help.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.940
My mother was more mad at me for getting help,

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.080
than the fact that I tried to end my life.

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:33.360
[Breathes shakily]

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.360
Sorry, just

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:42.920
Yesterday actually marked 10 years that my mom left

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:46.180
me and my dad, and after she left is

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:51.740
when I started battling with depression and anxiety and just like abandonment issues

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:55.680
and with that going on I actually,

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.820
attempted suicide also,

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:01.320
because I felt like if my own mom

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:05.880
Didn't want to stay with me then, what is the purpose of being here?

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:11.940
I feel for this person because they wanted to end their life after they fought with their mom.

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:16.120
I hope their relationship with their mother is good now,

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:17.440
and

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.880
that they got the help that they needed.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.100
When I came out to my parents as gay,

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:25.900
they told me to keep my mouth shut

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:28.820
and not tell anyone because they could ruin the family name.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:33.020
They chose reputation over their own child's happiness.

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:36.060
So,

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:40.000
because of my background, I'm Nigerian.

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:47.860
I'm coming from a culture that doesn't just not celebrate it but discourages it can be especially difficult

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:48.760
[sighs]

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:53.040
The best thing is to find your chosen family.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:56.880
To find people that will support you and love you unconditionally,

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.980
because, you know you have to,

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.600
navigate this crazy world with people on your side.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:03.520
Ah, It's unfortunate

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.340
if it can't be your bloodline,

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:08.140
but there are people, you should know that will support you.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:13.391
You just really got to pay attention to who you bring into your life,

00:07:13.391 --> 00:07:15.460
the type of people they're around as well.

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:19.460
Someone who's your friend really, is someone who looks out for you.

